      "stylistic_components": [
        {
          "id": "t-h",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "Android \u2014 where does cold start time actually go?",
            "variant": "h2"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t-p",
          "text_component": {
            "text": "app_cold_start is opened at the end of ShoppingDemoApp.onCreate(), back-dated to process start. Note the Android-specific conversion: appStartUptimeMs is SystemClock.uptimeMillis() (monotonic), but the SDK feeds a custom span start time into LogAttributesOverrides.OccurredAt, an epoch timestamp \u2014 passing uptime straight through would stamp the span in 1970. Three children nest under the root: sdk_init (Logger.start + config), scene_render (Compose standing the activity up through the startup effect), state_restore (demo prefs/flag bookkeeping). Same span names as iOS bd-shop-20.",
            "variant": "p"
          },
          "dashboard_layout_settings": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 3,
            "column_span": 12,
            "row_span": 8
          }
        },
